The following has been sitting on my blackboard forever, for about a month:

 * Move Var Serialization to struct type names instead of constants. More
   flexible and easier to debug.
 * Use `__LINE__` for integral values perhaps?
 * Support bitfields or generic `&/sizeof()`.
 * Need super custom as well.
 * Super or interface cannot be a proxy.

The first, is moving walking/serialization for dumps to be less manual and
to effectively be as automatic as possible. Duplicating all of the structure
members along with their types is just untenable. Of course this is only for
VM snapshots and save states.

The second, this is related to generic serialization. Effectively to detect
changed types or structure info, they are tied to their source line.

The third, instead of having custom handlers for the primitive data types and
for enumerations, use a generic integral handler.

The fourth, this should be a rare only case for serialization where if a type
really needs very specific handling to be serialized/deserialized.

The fifth, unrelated, a sanity measure for proxies.

